From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cix: adapt vendor drivers to Linux 7.2 APIs

The vendor drivers carried by this series were written for Linux 7.0 and
use kernel APIs that were removed or renamed in 7.2:

- clk: clk_ops.round_rate removed -> .determine_rate with
  divider_determine_rate() (clk-sky1-audss).
- drm: struct drm_atomic_state renamed to struct drm_atomic_commit,
  drm_atomic_state_put() -> drm_atomic_commit_put().
- drm: DRM_COLOR_FORMAT_* bitmasks replaced by the drm_output_color_format
  enum; display_info.color_formats is now a mask of
  BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_*), which has the same values (BIT(0..3)).
- drm: drm_atomic_private_obj_init() no longer takes an initial state;
  linlondp private objects get an .atomic_create_state hook (same pattern
  as upstream komeda).
- drm: drm_panel_init() removed -> devm_drm_panel_alloc() (cix_edp_panel).
- media: strncpy() removed -> strscpy() (amvx).

No functional change intended.

[added for Linux 7.2 by BOOKWORM]
---
 15 files changed, 226 insertions(+), 171 deletions(-)

